investigators in Mexico are trying to  determine the cause of an explosion on  board a ferry in Playa del Carmen on the  Caribbean coast surveillance cameras  captured the moment of the blast  yesterday as many as 25 people were hurt  on the dock including at least seven  Americans vladimir duthiers our  streaming network cbsn is here with the  details of the story from survivors who  are talking bad good morning good  morning Playa del Carmen is a popular  vacation destination a picturesque  resort town along the water one American  family of four was there on a beach  getaway when their trip took a  terrifying turn security camera footage  shows the moment a fireball ripped  through the center of the ferry the boat  had just docked at the beach town of  Playa del Carmen passengers were still  disembarking when the explosion sent  debris and shrapnel into the water and  the crowd emergency crews rushed to the  scene and tended to the injured Mexican  officials say 18 people were taken to  the hospital images of the aftermath  show a gaping hole in the center of the  ship Rebecca and Steve Long's family  were on the dock waiting for another  ferry to Cozumel when the blast happened  the couple's two young sons suffered  minor cuts and bruises from the  explosion they were taken to the  hospital where they receive stitches and  were released  thankfully no one was killed  local officials say preliminary reports  indicate the explosion was due to  mechanical failure a deeper  investigation into exactly what caused  that failure is ongoing looking at those  pictures it's hard to believe nobody was  killed it was edible explosion that's  amazing Thank You Vlad
 

